  m_Name: Readme
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  icon: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 2a883f4c030cbad44a2565919e1a208b, type: 3}
  title: How to use scenes
  sections:
  - heading: Game
    text: This scene is used for building the game, and contains all the logic, UI,
      visuals and other content necessary to play the game. It works solely with
      the GameInitializer, which instantiates everything that is needed to make the
      game run (supposedly). You can switch the game profile for another one if you
      want to test the game with ddifferent configurations. Be careful not to modify
      the main game profile if you're not sure of what you're doing !
    linkText: 
    url: 
  - heading: Dev Scenes
    text: In this folder, you can create all the scenes you want to work on specific
      features, that will not directly be reflected in the game. You can use it to
      test stuff. You can also duplicate and rename the main scene there, to start
      from the current latest version of the game.
    linkText: 
    url: 
  - heading: Backup
    text: In this folder, we can backup the MainScene, to make sure that prior versions
      of the game are saved. This doesn't mean it will always work, since changes
      to prefabs will be reflected in these scenes too !
    linkText: 
    url: 
  loadedLayout: 1
